{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SCOPE CORRECTION FROM THE IMPLEMENTER, and it materially changes this ticket: the pytest-only repo-invariant gate class is approximately SEVENTY modules, not the three I named. The three in my description are simply the ones that bit me in one night. The wider population includes CI/workflow parity checks, ratchet baseline-vs-tree checks, public-surface censuses, generated-artifact and docs drift gates, and whole-tree AST policy scans.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: my proposed resolution #1 -- 'a fast make check-gates that runs exactly these ratchet/parity tests and nothing else' -- WAS WRONG. A curated node list would be a second list to keep in sync with that population, i.e. the same drift defect one level up. That is the identical error pattern this repository has produced repeatedly (740d's hand-registered fixture allowlist, 2593's hard-coded builder list, the ADR .numbers markers), and I proposed it while having just documented that pattern. Worth noting against my own judgement, not just the tree's.\n\nCHOSEN RESOLUTION: 'make verify' = lint + typecheck + test, documented in AGENTS.md as the pre-push contract. Complete BY CONSTRUCTION -- make test already carries exactly CI's DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS ('not integration and not external'), so nothing is enumerated and nothing can drift. make lint and the pre-commit hook are untouched, so the tight loop keeps its 27s. A Makefile target is not a ci_gate under the mechanism scanner (that kind covers scripts/check_*.py files and workflow run: steps), so no ratchet trip is expected.\n\nMeasured so far on this host (18 logical / 6 performance cores): make lint 27s, make typecheck 10s, the three named gate tests 67s serial and 11.6s under -n 4 --dist worksteal. Full-suite timing still being measured.\n\nAC3 mechanics validated in a throwaway repo: 'git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard' sees a written-but-unstaged scripts/check_*.py that the current tracked-only listing misses, while still excluding gitignored paths -- a strictly WIDENING change that can only turn a false green red, never the reverse.\n\nOPEN CONCERN I have raised with the implementer rather than left implicit: the full default suite is ~15-20 minutes in CI. A pre-push contract that long risks being skipped under time pressure, and a contract people skip fails exactly as badly as the false-green one it replaces -- just differently. Asked for the measured wall-clock (serial and parallel) to be documented plainly where the target is named, so a contributor plans for it rather than killing it and losing trust in the target."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788513814491058001,"uuid":"1f71b7be-76b0-4696-a07a-b8f3712a8378"}